{
    "background_story": "Elodie was a devout young woman living in 17th-century Salem, Massachusetts. Born into a family of strict Puritan values, she was raised to believe in the importance of hard work, simplicity, and moral rectitude. Elodie's days were filled with prayer, household chores, and scripture study. She was especially drawn to the teachings of John Calvin, which emphasized the concept of predestination. As a result, Elodie believed that her life's path was predetermined by God, and she strove to live a life of utmost piety and obedience. Her community respected her for her unwavering commitment to their shared values, and she became a model of Puritan virtue. Despite the challenges and hardships of her time, Elodie remained steadfast in her faith, believing that her strict adherence to Puritan principles would ultimately lead her to salvation.",
